  "question": {
    "text": "A deflection magnetometer is placed with its arm along the east-west direction and a bar magnet is placed along the arm of the magnetometer. Due to the magnet, the deflection observed is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math>&nbsp;and the period of oscillation of the needle in the magnetometer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>. When the magnet is removed, the period of oscillation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. The relation between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> is",
