  "solution": {
    "text": "In the usual setting of deflection magnetometer, field due to magnet (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>) and horizontal component (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>) of earth&#39;s field are perpendicular to each other. Therefore, the net field on the magnetic needle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math> ...(i)<br /><br />When the magnet is removed,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi>MH</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math> ...(ii)<br /><br />Also, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></math><br /><br />Dividing (i) by (ii), we get<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><msqrt><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8756;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math>",
